.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH AMU\-BIN 8
.SH NAME
amu\-bin \- Qwaderton Linux package manager (sole spm frontend)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBamu\-bin\fR is the binary package manager for Qwaderton Linux and the
\fBonly\fR tool that operates on installed packages and the spm(8)
database. It installs, upgrades and removes \fI.spm\fR packages, fetches
pre-built binaries from a binary repository, and resolves dependencies.
.LP
There is no package index and no database to sync: package metadata
(name, version, dependencies, description, install scripts) is read
directly from the recipe repositories in \fBAMU_REPO\fR, which are
synchronized with \fBreposync\fR(8). This makes the recipe repositories
the single source of truth for both \fBamu\-src\fR(8) and \fBamu\-bin\fR.
.LP
The binary repository \fBAMU_BINREPO\fR is a plain HTTP(S)/FTP server or
local directory holding \fIname#version-release.spm\fR files with
optional \fI.spm.sha3\fR sidecar checksum files. The package file name
is derived from the recipe, so no separate index is needed.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR \fI<target...>\fR
Install. Each target is either an existing \fI.spm\fR file, installed
directly, or a package name, resolved against \fBAMU_REPO\fR together
with its full dependency closure, downloaded from \fBAMU_BINREPO\fR,
verified against the \fI.spm.sha3\fR sidecar, and installed. Already
installed packages are skipped. Prompts for confirmation unless
\fBAMU_NOPROMPT\fR is set. Requires root.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR \fI<target...>\fR
Upgrade or reinstall specific targets. File targets are upgraded
directly; name targets are re-downloaded from \fBAMU_BINREPO\fR using
the version from the recipe (reinstalls if already up to date). No
dependency resolution, no confirmation prompt. Requires root.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR \fI<name...>\fR
Remove packages. Plain removal, no dependency analysis: refuses if the
package is required by another installed package (spm safety), otherwise
removes just the named packages. Requires root.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR \fI<name...>\fR
Remove packages together with their dependencies that become unneeded.
A target that still has installed dependents outside the removal set is
skipped. Prompts for confirmation unless \fBAMU_NOPROMPT\fR is set.
Requires root.
.TP
\fB\-U\fR
Full system upgrade. Compares every installed package against the
version in its recipe (skipping \fBAMU_MASK\fR), resolves the dependency
closure of the outdated set, installs new dependencies first, then
upgrades. Prompts for confirmation unless \fBAMU_NOPROMPT\fR is set.
Requires root.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fI<name...>\fR
Download packages into \fBAMU_CACHE_DIR\fR without installing.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR
Clean the download cache: remove cached \fI.spm\fR files whose checksum
does not match their \fI.spm.sha3\fR sidecar.
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR [\fIpattern\fR]
List installed packages, optionally filtered by name pattern.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fI<pkg>\fR
List the files installed by \fI<pkg>\fR.
.TP
\fB\-O\fR \fI<file>\fR
Print the installed package that owns \fI<file>\fR.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR [\fIpattern\fR]
Search available packages in the recipe repositories. Without a pattern,
lists all packages. With \fB\-v\fR, prints name, version and description.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR \fI<output.spm>\fR
Package the current directory (a populated fakeroot) into the named
\fI.spm\fR file. Low-level helper used by \fBamu\-src\fR(8); wraps
\fBspm \-b\fR.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Verbose output (with \fB\-s\fR).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Print help and exit.

.SH INSTALLATION PIPELINE
.LP
For every package it installs or upgrades, \fBamu\-bin\fR runs, in
order: the recipe's \fIpreinstall\fR script (chrooted under
\fBAMU_ROOT\fR when set), \fBspm \-i\fR/\fBspm \-u\fR, the recipe's
\fIpostinstall\fR script, and \fBamu\-trigger\fR(8) for the package.
\fBamu\-src\fR(8) delegates installation to this pipeline, so source
builds and binary installs behave identically on the target system.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBAMU_BINREPO\fR
Binary repository URL (http://, https://, ftp://) or local path.
Required for name-based installs and upgrades.
.TP
\fBAMU_CACHE_DIR\fR
Directory for downloaded \fI.spm\fR files. Required.
.TP
\fBAMU_REPO\fR
Space-separated recipe repository directories. Source of truth for
versions and dependencies.
.TP
\fBAMU_ROOT\fR
Alternative install root (default \fI/\fR).
.TP
\fBAMU_NOPROMPT\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fBAMU_MASK\fR
Packages skipped during \fB\-U\fR.
.TP
\fBAMU_ALIAS\fR
Dependency substitution, \fIreal:alias\fR pairs.
.TP
\fBAMU_STRICT\fR
Fail instead of warning when a downloaded package has no \fI.spm.sha3\fR
sidecar.

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI$AMU_CACHE_DIR\fR
Downloaded package cache.
.TP
\fI${AMU_ROOT}/var/lib/spm/db\fR
Installed package database (owned by spm).
.TP
\fI/etc/amu.conf\fR
System-wide configuration, sourced by the amu library.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amu (8),
.BR amu\-src (8),
.BR amu\-resolv (8),
.BR amu\-trigger (8),
.BR reposync (8),
.BR spm (8)

